      "source": "SAC Route Portal",
      "notes_html": "<p>Right at the beginning you need to scramble up a tiered ramp (faint path, at the end slightly exposed, grade I). Then follows a long rocky rib with more grade I passages. The summit ridge is made of blocks, and in early summer it is often snow-covered. Then an ice axe might come in handy. On its most important passages the route is well marked.</p>"
